---
// PastePerfect's privacy policy: the Privacy Policy URL for the App Store listing. Mirrors WorldBar's.
// It describes only what the app does. Keep it in step with the app if that changes.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const EMAIL = 'njvanderbyl@gmail.com';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy · PastePerfect"
  description="PastePerfect collects no personal data, has no accounts and makes no network requests. Clipboard text stays on your Mac."
  image="/og/pasteperfect.jpg"
  imageAlt="PastePerfect: copy anything, paste perfectly."
>
  <article class="doc shell">
    <p class="doc__crumb t-annotation"><a href={`${base}pasteperfect/`}>PastePerfect</a> · Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="doc__title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="doc__meta t-annotation">Effective 22 November 2026 · Applies to the PastePerfect app for Mac</p>

    <div class="doc__panel">
      <p>
        <strong>The short version.</strong> PastePerfect has no accounts and no servers. It does not collect, send or
        share any personal data. The text you copy stays on your Mac.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      PastePerfect is made and published by an independent developer.
      Contact: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=PastePerfect%20privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What PastePerfect does not do</h2>
    <p>
      It has no sign-in, no analytics, no advertising, no crash reporting, no third-party code and no tracking of
      any kind. The app runs in the macOS App Sandbox without network access, so it cannot send anything off your
      Mac. Cleaning works offline.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What it does with your clipboard</h2>
    <p>
      PastePerfect reads the clipboard only when you open its window, bring the app forward, press the reload
      button, or use the shortcut or Clean Clipboard. It does not watch the clipboard in the background. It
      changes the text on your Mac and writes the result back to the clipboard as plain text. It keeps no history,
      and it does not save your clipboard to disk or send it anywhere. Images and files on the clipboard are never
      read or cleared.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What is stored on your Mac</h2>
    <p>
      Your settings only: which cleaning options are on, the URL mode and custom rules, your keyboard shortcut,
      launch at login and appearance. They are saved in the app's own preferences inside its sandbox container.
      Deleting the app's data removes them. They are never synced or uploaded.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Permissions</h2>
    <p>
      PastePerfect does not request access to your contacts, calendar, location, files, photos, camera or
      microphone. The global shortcut uses a standard macOS hot key and needs no accessibility or input monitoring
      permission.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Launch at login</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn this on, PastePerfect uses the macOS login item system. That setting is managed by macOS and is
      visible in System Settings, General, Login Items.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If PastePerfect ever changes how it handles data, I will update this page and the effective date above
      before the change ships.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=PastePerfect%20privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="doc__links t-annotation">
      <a href={`${base}pasteperfect/`}>PastePerfect</a> · <a href={`${base}pasteperfect/support/`}>Support</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    scroll-snap-type: none !important;
  }

  :global(.site-header) {
    position: static !important;
  }

  .doc {
    padding-block: 56px 112px;
    max-width: calc(820px + 2 * var(--pad));
  }

  .doc__crumb {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .doc__crumb a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .doc__crumb a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .doc__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .doc__lede,
  .doc__meta {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .doc__panel {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-pasteperfect);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(80% 120% at 100% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-pasteperfect) 14%, transparent), transparent 70%),
      var(--color-surface);
  }

  .doc__panel p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 36px 0 10px;
  }

  article p {
    max-width: 66ch;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .doc__panel p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .doc__links {
    margin-top: 48px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
</style>
